{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The WAGO connectors and Wirefy adhesive-lined tubing felt useful because they complement my existing spade connectors: they offer another way to join wires and a way to insulate and seal those connections.",
    "The Gorilla patch tape connects naturally to my previous Gorilla tape purchases while offering waterproof patching for a different repair need, although the white color limits where I would use it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The large-diameter XHF tubing is too specific for a need I have not shown; being useful for wiring does not mean its size fits my repairs.",
    "Electronic cleaner and a deburring tool assume tasks I do not currently have. Using wire connectors does not imply cleaning contacts, and buying hose clamps does not imply cutting pipes."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair supplies seem to have been taken as interest in almost any electrical or plumbing accessory, even when the item serves a different task.",
    "My previous connector purchase seems to suggest that I need more connector assortments, although wire taps would only be useful if I needed that particular kind of connection."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more interested in supplies that add a useful capability to what I already own, such as sealing connections, than in another assortment with no immediate purpose.",
    "Practical fit matters: tubing diameter, tape color, and whether a repair actually requires precise measuring or waterproof sealing affect whether I would choose an otherwise relevant item now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my practical repair interests, but sometimes assumed specific repair tasks from supplies I had bought."
}"}
